    TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentActivity.Tests.swift:103 (neither touched by me). To
    obtain test evidence I applied a TEMPORARY verification-only rename to the feature-views
    copy, ran the suite, then `git checkout`-restored it — the working tree is clean and
    NO out-of-scope file is committed.
  • macOS app target build is blocked ONLY by dev-certificate code-signing of the macOS
    widget extension (env/signing), not by any code; the iOS-Simulator build needs no signing
    and is GREEN. Per ADR-002 both idioms share the one `Sources/` group, so the GREEN iOS
    build + GREEN macOS-capable Swift-6 type-check (harness) cover both.

